<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Democratic Republic of Vietnam</h1><p class="st-meta">1945 CE – 1976 CE · capital Hanoi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The communist-led Vietnamese state proclaimed by Ho Chi Minh in 1945, which defeated France, fought the Vietnam War and reunified the country in 1976.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/august-revolution">August Revolution</a> of 1945 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a>, a front led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochinese-communist-party">Indochinese Communist Party</a>, seized power across much of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/socialist-republic-of-vietnam">Vietnam</a>. On 2 September 1945 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh">Ho Chi Minh</a> read the declaration of independence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ba-dinh-square">Ba Dinh Square</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a>, proclaiming the Democratic <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-vietnam">Republic of Vietnam</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The DRV fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-indochina-war">First Indochina War</a> from 1946, winning at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dien-bien-phu">Dien Bien Phu</a> in 1954. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-geneva">Geneva</a> Accords left it in control of the north above the 17th parallel. It built a one-party socialist state with collectivised agriculture after a harsh land reform, backed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, and supported the southern insurgency through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh-trail">Ho Chi Minh Trail</a> against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-vietnam">Republic of Vietnam</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris-peace-accords">Paris Peace Accords</a> of 1973 and the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh-city">Saigon</a> in April 1975, the DRV merged with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-south-vietnam">Republic of South Vietnam</a>. On 2 July 1976 the united country was proclaimed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/socialist-republic-of-vietnam">Socialist Republic of Vietnam</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/democratic-republic-of-vietnam.jpg" alt="Democratic Republic of Vietnam" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: See File History below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_North_Vietnam_(1955%E2%80%931976).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1945 CE – 1976 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hanoi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ho Chi Minh, Le Duan, Pham Van Dong</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>State atheism, Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Vietnamese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/vietnam">Vietnam</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>North Vietnam, DRV</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1960&amp;focus=democratic-republic-of-vietnam" aria-label="Democratic Republic of Vietnam on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7526 1400 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Democratic Republic of Vietnam lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7846 1656L7930 1822M7846 1656L7846 1656M7846 1656L7939 2031"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7930 1822h0M7846 1656h0M7939 2031h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7846 1656h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7846 1656h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Hanoi. <a href="/atlas?year=1960&amp;focus=democratic-republic-of-vietnam">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
